# Line endings are CONTENT here, not formatting.
#
# The 2026-07-26 platform probe (this family's first non-Linux CI run) failed
# `evals-governance > MANIFEST.sha256 matches the current evals/ content` on
# Windows: git's autocrlf checkout rewrote LF to CRLF, the bytes changed, and a
# tamper-evidence hash computed over those bytes could never match. The manifest
# is deliberately a hash of raw bytes — weakening it to normalize line endings
# would blunt exactly what it exists to detect — so the checkout is pinned
# instead.
#
# Default: every text file checks out with LF on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary-ish assets git must never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.tgz binary
*.jsonl.gz binary
